00:37:18,100 --> 00:37:20,100
So let's talk a little bit about each of these

705
00:37:21,100 --> 00:37:24,100
three, first the Geometrical Optics.

706
00:37:24,100 --> 00:37:25,100
So that's the course,

707
00:37:25,100 --> 00:37:29,100
that's a continuation of our introduction to photonics class.

708
00:37:29,100 --> 00:37:33,100
Here we are focusing on different types of optical components

709
00:37:33,100 --> 00:37:37,100
such as mirrors, lenses, prisms.

710
00:37:37,100 --> 00:37:40,100
We are trying to see how we can manipulate the light

711
00:37:40,100 --> 00:37:44,100
by using these types of optical components.

712
00:37:44,100 --> 00:37:47,100
We are also going to make it a real world

713
00:37:47,100 --> 00:37:49,100
and as practical as possible.

714
00:37:49,100 --> 00:37:51,100
We're going to talk about binoculars,

715
00:37:51,100 --> 00:37:54,100
we're going to talk about telescopes.

716
00:37:54,100 --> 00:37:59,100
We are going to talk about why the soap bubbles

717
00:37:59,100 --> 00:38:03,100
would have those beautiful rainbow colors.

718
00:38:03,100 --> 00:38:06,100
We are going to talk about 3D polarizing glasses

719
00:38:06,100 --> 00:38:09,100
and many other different types of applications

720
00:38:09,100 --> 00:38:14,100
of this type of material.

721
00:38:14,100 --> 00:38:18,100
The Fiber Optics course focuses on the aspect

722
00:38:18,100 --> 00:38:20,100
