Pre-requisite for this course is an introduction

741
00:39:26,100 --> 00:39:31,100
to photonics course that you are finalizing right now.

742
00:39:31,100 --> 00:39:36,100
In this course that is labeled Laser Technologies

743
00:39:36,100 --> 00:39:40,100
we are going to be operating on types of lasers

744
00:39:40,100 --> 00:39:43,100
that are kind of more advanced,

745
00:39:43,100 --> 00:39:46,100
especially Class 3B and Class 4 lasers.

746
00:39:46,100 --> 00:39:49,100
We're going to be performing a whole bunch of experiments

747
00:39:49,100 --> 00:39:52,100
using different types of equipment such as beam profilers,

748
00:39:52,100 --> 00:39:55,100
spectrometers, and some other.

749
00:39:55,100 --> 00:39:57,100
So it's an advanced level class

750
00:39:57,100 --> 00:40:00,100
where you're going to be exposed to different types of lasers

751
00:40:00,100 --> 00:40:03,100
starting with basic helium neon lasers,

752
00:40:03,100 --> 00:40:05,100
going over laser diodes,

753
00:40:05,100 --> 00:40:08,100
talking about CO2 lasers, fiber lasers,

754
00:40:08,100 --> 00:40:11,100
and the YAG lasers, disk lasers, etc.

755
00:40:12,100 --> 00:40:14,100
So in all advanced level class

756
00:40:14,100 --> 00:40:17,100
that's going to give you a very nice set of skills

757
00:40:17,100 --> 00:40:20,100
to work in some of the coolest places

758
00:40:20,100 --> 00:40:25,100
that are operating these types of lasers.

